{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nAfter S2, command identity/help and every handler grammar come from the registry/parser system, but real execution still traverses explicit intercept/dispatch ladders and policy frozensets. Leaving those selection authorities in parallel preserves the coordination defect RP-05 is intended to remove.\n\n## Approach\nMove core top-level execution to the selected registry route after the pre-operation help boundary. Resolve only the selected lazy handler reference and invoke it through a closed typed adapter-kind set matching existing call shapes. The router passes the original command remainder unchanged; the selected handler uses S2's shared argparse factory. The router must not parse command/nested options a second time.\n\nConsume route metadata for:\n\n- central best-effort mount eligibility;\n- strict initialization `none`, `init_only`, or `full`, plus narrow pure selectors for genuinely conditional cases;\n- position-independent confirmation/output extraction while preserving tokens after `--`;\n- legacy output passthrough for `create`, `idea`, `transition`, `claim`, and `reopen`;\n- exact handler adapter, argv, stdout/stderr, exit-code, and exception contracts.\n\nBefore cutover, compare registry-derived policies and selected handler/parser pairs to every existing set and arm. Any non-allowlisted delta fails shadow parity. Cut over one selection authority only after parity is exact; keep derived compatibility exports for S6 rollback.\n\nThis story covers core and bridge execution that does not change optional-capability posture. S4 owns selected optional mode/backend checks and may proceed from the same S2 contract without editing dispatch.\n\n## Compatibility and Rollback\nThe positive rationale is a single validated selection/dispatch authority while preserving specialized parser-backed handlers. No signature introspection, middleware pipeline, eager parser-tree construction, or second parse is added. Rollback selects the derived compatibility exports; no event, ticket, bridge, or binding data changes.\n\n## Testing\nUse real CLI subprocess contracts rather than source greps. Extend mount/init, mutation confirmation, global output, bridge vocabulary, hidden alias, unknown, and exit-code suites. Add typed fake handlers for every adapter kind/selector. Include negative controls for tokens after `--`, malformed global flags, no-auto-mount commands, store-touching intercepts, handler exceptions, and a parser spy proving the selected handler parses exactly once while unrelated factories/handlers are not imported.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Every core canonical command and compatibility spelling resolves exactly one lazy handler through a closed adapter kind, and only the selected handler/parser modules are imported.\n- [ ] The top-level router preserves original remainder argv and the selected S2 factory parses it exactly once; no route-level option grammar exists.\n- [ ] Registry-derived mount/init behavior matches the pre-cutover census for every route, including no-auto-mount and conditional cases.\n- [ ] Confirmation, global output extraction, legacy JSON shapes, `--`, streams, exit codes, and exception propagation match existing behavioral tests.\n- [ ] Bridge compatibility spellings and hidden `bridge-status` execute through approved adapters while `purge-bridge` remains unknown.\n- [ ] Execution can switch back to derived compatibility exports without handler, generated-help, or persisted-data changes."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787070720600931001,"uuid":"ded2ca48-1e24-4759-aa88-c14ddecbb214"}